1551..1622 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
1623..1696 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
1697..1774 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
1775..1841 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `Path.step(loop ∷ p, q)` is"
1842..1918 Comment "/// `loop ∷ Path.step(p, q)`. At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the"
1919..1986 Comment "/// empty word, and the composite over it runs that call first; the"
1987..2051 Comment "/// composites the arms carry convert through their definitions."
